	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"The &dGoety&r mod is a &bmagic&r mod designed to enhance the Minecraft experience by adding a wide range of new features, including mobs, structures, and methods of harnessing arcane power."
				""
				"&2Summon various minions&r, &5brew legendary potions&r, &3perform rituals&r, &4master the Illagers' Magic&r, and uncover the world’s secrets, legends, and treasures!"
				""
				"The mod’s &6guidebook&r will &2gradually unlock new entries as you progress through the mod&r, so be sure to check it from time to time for &2newly added content&r."
				""
				"&7——For a long time, you have been curious about the dark magic of Illagers, especially Evokers. What inspires their power? Beyond granting a way to cheat death, what else can their Totems do? How does one achieve such feats?&r"
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1b
				id: "patchouli:guide_book"
				tag: {
					"patchouli:book": "goety:black_book"
				}
			}
			id: "39A1A046832960CC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "25C36F05EB7EC240"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "patchouli:guide_book"
					tag: {
						"patchouli:book": "goety:black_book"
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "octagon"
			subtitle: "We know very little about their power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2576554D1A4F255C"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Origin of the Illagers' Magic"
			x: 1.5d
			y: -0.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["38C7544366E690D9"]
			description: [
				"The &6Totem of Roots&r is an early-game item in the mod used to store and utilize &bSoul Energy&r."
				""
				"When placed in your hotbar or accessory slot, it will accumulate &bSoul Energy&r whenever you &ekill mobs&r."
				""
				"The &6Totem of Roots&r can hold up to &2100 Soul Energy&r."
				""
				"&7Different mobs contain different amounts of Soul Energy. Villagers, in particular, contain relatively high amounts.&r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &6Totem of Roots&r can be used in a &6Crafting Table&r to create &2Haunted Saplings, Empty Focuses, Awakened Emeralds, Cursed Metal Ingots, Savage Tooth, and Shade Stones.&r"
				""
				"&7Hover over the Totem of Roots and press U (Show Uses) to view related recipes.&r"
			]
			id: "38E0930B64874596"
			rewards: [{
				id: "5CAC76DDA55E46F5"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Hunt for souls"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2D7682B930A92B64"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "goety:totem_of_roots"
					tag: {
						"Max Souls": 100
						Souls: 0
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -3.5d
			y: -0.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["38E0930B64874596"]
			description: [
				"Once you obtain the &6Totem of Roots&r, you can use the &bSoul Energy&r stored within it to craft special items—such as the &aAwakened Emerald&r."
				""
				"Using the &2Awakened Emerald&r as a crafting ingredient, you can create a replica of the Totem of Undying, the &6Totem of Souls&r."
				""
				"It has a storage capacity of &e10,000 Soul Energy&r and can function like a vanilla Totem of Undying, &esaving you from a fatal blow once&r. &7(It only works when fully charged, and will be completely drained upon activation.)&r"
			]
			id: "2E3C5A01C7C079C0"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2FE5AB17C6996C58"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "More soul energy"
			tasks: [{
				id: "341804E4A14147C2"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "goety:totem_of_souls"
					tag: {
						"Max Souls": 10000
						Souls: 0
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -3.5d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["39A1A046832960CC"]
			description: [
				"&7Although using the Totems to craft cursed items is convenient, you now have a more cheaper method.&r"
				""
				"The &6Cursed Infuser&r is crafted using vanilla materials. It must be placed &2above any mob spawner&r to function. When activated, right-click the &6Cursed Infuser&r with specific items, and after a few seconds it will produce the corresponding cursed output."
				""
				"If the center of the Cursed Infuser is glowing, it means it is activated and ready for use. &7(As shown, the left infuser is inactive, while the right one is successfully activated.)&r"
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/goety_2.png width:72 height:50 align:1}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The relationships between items and their cursed infused counterparts are as follows:"
				""
				"Stone and its variants — &5Shade Stone&r"
				"Bone Block — &5Savage Tooth&r"
				"Amethyst Shard — &5Empty Focus&r"
				"Any Sapling — &5Haunted Sapling&r"
				"Emerald — &5Awakened Emerald&r"
				"Iron Ingot — &5Cursed Metal Ingot&r"
				"Iron Block — &5Block of Cursed Metal&r"
				"Witch Hat / Illusive Robe / Warlock Robe / Witch Robe — &5Their corresponding cursed variants&r"
			]
			id: "4717C67580F37824"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2BDFA8D3D122088A"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Cheaper way for curse infusion"
			tasks: [{
				id: "29B8FCA6003ACBCF"
				item: "goety:cursed_infuser"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 1.5d
			y: 1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["37315B135F29355E"]
			description: [
				"Now you can attempt to perform rituals to gain new powers. You will need a &6Dark Altar&r and several &6Pedestals&r."
				""
				"First, prepare a &6Cursed Cage&r containing &esoul energy&r, then place the &6Dark Altar&r directly &2above the Cursed Cage&r."
				""
				"If the &6Dark Altar&r &2lights up with a green glow&r and emits dark particles, it means the ritual has been successfully activated and is ready for use. (as shown below)"
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/goety_3.png width:70 height:60 align:1}"
			]
			icon: "goety:dark_altar"
			id: "249B296A3CB17779"
			rewards: [{
				count: 3
				id: "6BDC89223CDF05F0"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
