		{
			dependencies: ["24119BB18C19CC04"]
			description: [
				"This quest will guide you in brewing a &dPotion for Woodcutting&r, while also &2explaining the details and workflow of Witch’s Brewing&r throughout the process."
				""
				"&7(Please turn the page to view each step and its explanations.)&r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Failure is the Mother of Success · Brewing Failure&r"
				""
				"To successfully brew potions, you must understand what brewing failure looks like and how to handle it. If brewing fails, the liquid inside the cauldron will turn &2dark brown&r and begin &2emitting black smoke&r."
				""
				"Failed brews can be handled by bottling them into a &6Bottle of Refuce&r, or by sneaking and right-clicking the cauldron with a wand or wooden stick to clear it."
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/goety_7.png width:60 height:60 align:1}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 1 · Capacity&r"
				""
				"Capacity come in many forms and &emust be added in order&r. For this brew, we only need the &cbasics&r: &cNether Wart&r."
				""
				"Drop a single &cNether Wart&r into a heated, water-filled &6Witch’s Cauldron&r. &7(Only one can be added!)&r"
				""
				"If done correctly, the cauldron will emit &dpurple particles&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 2 · Catalyst&r"
				""
				"Catalysts in Witch’s Brewing can vary greatly. In this case, we need a &6Stone Axe&r."
				""
				"Drop the &6Stone Axe&r into the cauldron."
				""
				"If successful, the liquid will turn &2light brown&r and continue emitting &dpurple particles&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Completion&r"
				""
				"Since this potion does not require additional complexity, we &2skip the Augmentation step&r. &7(In Witch’s Brewing, only the  Augmentation step can be skipped.)&r"
				""
				"Use a &6Cauldron Ladle&r to right-click the Witch’s Cauldron to start brewing. Then use a &6glass bottle&r to collect the potion, and &2drink it near a tree&r, you will understand its effect！"
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1b
				id: "minecraft:potion"
				tag: {
					Potion: "minecraft:water"
				}
			}
			id: "28B168188F040792"
			rewards: [{
				count: 5
				id: "13A6A8D1EFC3D7DC"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "A little test"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5231888AFEEE6077"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The First Brew"
			x: -3.75d
			y: 8.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["28B168188F040792"]
			description: [
				"&cStep 1 · Capacity · Explanation&r"
				""
				"when adding the ingredients, a strict &2fixed order&r must be followed, and each one provides a set amount of capacity. "
				""
				"&7The value in ( ) indicates capacity provided.&r"
				""
				"&bNether Wart (+4) → Crimson Fungus (+2) → Snap Warts (+2) → Awakened Emerald (+2) → Concentrated Emerald (+2) → Ruby of Souls (+4)&r"
				""
				"You &2must add the ingredients in the exact order listed above&r. For example, if you want a potion with 6 capacity, you must first add a Nether Wart, then a Crimson Fungus. Otherwise, the brewing process will &4fail&r."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1b
				id: "minecraft:potion"
				tag: {
