		{
			dependencies: [
				"41D89F8681CF24E9"
				"6670071A9FBD1EF1"
				"2669B7A8FC8D1A59"
			]
			description: [
				"This quest will guide you in brewing a &2rather “unique” potion&r, allowing you to learn &2all the basic mechanics&r of Witch’s Brewing through the process."
				""
				"&c——Preparation · Check Required Capacity&r"
				"This potion requires two &cCatalysts&r: &6Beetroot Soup&r and &6Honeycomb&r. You can check their &2effects&r and &2capacity costs&r in the &cGuidebook&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 1 · Sufficient Capacity &r"
				""
				"This potion must be &2thrown&r, so the &cAugmentation step&r also requires adding &6Gunpowder&r. This brings the total required capacity to 6. &7(Beetroot Soup +3, Honeycomb +2, Gunpowder +1)&r"
				""
				"Therefore, the basic +4 capacity from Nether Wart is not enough. You must follow the previously mentioned order and add &6Nether Wart&r followed by &6Crimson Fungus&r to reach a total capacity of &e6&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 2 · Catalysts&r"
				""
				"In Witch’s Brewing, as long as you do not exceed the capacity limit, multiple catalysts can be added."
				""
				"After confirming the cauldron shows &e0/6&r capacity usage, add &6Beetroot Soup&r and &6Honeycomb&r. &7(No specific order required.)&r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 3 · Augmentation&r"
				""
				"You need to add &6Gunpowder&r to turn the potion into a &2Splash Potion&r. &7(This information can also be found in the Augmentation section of the Guidebook.)&r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c——Step 4 · Completion&r"
				""
				"If everything was done correctly, use the &6Cauldron Ladle&r to right-click the Witch’s Cauldron, infuse soul energy, and retrieve the potion."
				""
				"&dThrow the potion at hostile mobs to experience the true charm of Witch’s Brewing！&r"
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1b
				id: "goety:splash_brew"
