		{
			dependencies: ["249B296A3CB17779"]
			description: [
				"Performing different types of &dRituals&r also requires placing &2specific blocks in the correct types and quantities&r around the &6Dark Altar&r, or ensuring that the altar’s &2location meets certain conditions&r."
				""
				"&7If the coordinates of the Dark Altar are (X, Y, Z), the required altar bases and blocks may be placed anywhere within a cubic area from (X-8, Y-8, Z-8) to (X+8, Y+8, Z+8). (No placement order required.)&r"
				""
				"You may place &2multiple types of ritual-required blocks&r within the same Dark Altar detection range, allowing a single altar to support multiple rituals."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Once the placement requirements for a ritual are met, the player must first confirm the &2recipe of the item being crafted through that ritual&r."
				""
				"Start by right-clicking &6Pedestals&r with the required items to place them (no specific order or position required). When the type and quantity requirements are satisfied, hold the item to be placed into the &6Dark Altar&r and right-click the altar."
				""
				"If the &6Cursed Cage&r beneath the altar contains any Soul Energy, the ritual will begin."
				""
				"Each ritual consumes a different amount of Soul Energy. Be sure check the Cursed Cage beforehand to confirm whether it has enough Soul Energy. Otherwise, the &critual will fail, resulting in loss of items and Soul Energy&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As shown in the example, this setup combines both a &2Animation Ritual&r and a &2Forge Ritual&r."
				""
				"For crafting the &2Hunger Core&r, which depends on the Animation Ritual, you must first place the required items : &6Rotten Flesh&r, &6Meat items&r, &6Pufferfish&r, &6Soul Sand&r, and &6Savage Tooth&rinto the surrounding &6Pedestals&r. &7(as shown, no placement order required)&r"
				""
				"Then place the required &6Empty Focus&r into the central &6Dark Altar&r to begin the ritual crafting process."
				""
